  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "The current best (config_010: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.520) is only marginally ahead of rna_only (config_014, acc=0.514), suggesting the image modality's contribution is modest and may depend on how the RNA representation interacts with it. All four completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, so we have no evidence on whether an alternative encoder (scvi_n200, a variational autoencoder with 200-dim latent space) could improve multimodal fusion or reveal a stronger interaction with the image branch. config_045 changes only the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200 while keeping the otherwise-best settings (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile), making it a clean single-variable test. If scvi_n200 matches or beats scgpt, it opens a broader search space; if it underperforms, it confirms scgpt as the preferred encoder and lets us focus remaining budget on aggregation/fusion refinements around scgpt. With 5 experiments left, resolving this key design axis is the highest-value uncertainty reduction."
}

